-- title:
--   (B-8), App-19 — the cone {c ∈ ℝ^p : c′g_i ≥ 0} of η-separated unit vectors has µ ≤ √(1 − η^{2(p−1)}/p³)
-- statement:
--   Let $p\ge1$, $0<\eta\le1$, and let $g_1,\dots,g_p\in\mathbb R^p$ be unit vectors such that each vector after the first is far from the span of its predecessors:
--   $$\|g_i-\Pi_{g_1,\dots,g_{i-1}}(g_i)\|^2\ \ge\ \eta^2,\qquad i=2,\dots,p,$$
--   where $\Pi$ denotes orthogonal projection onto the span. Then the cone $K=\{c\in\mathbb R^p:\ c'g_i\ge0,\ i=1,\dots,p\}$ has circumradius
--   $$\mu(K)=\sin\alpha(K)\ \le\ \sqrt{1-\frac{\eta^{2(p-1)}}{p^3}}. \tag{B-8}$$
--
--   This is the core of Lemma 10 in the coordinates of the subspace: in the paper $g_i=B_{\Delta_{t+1}}\delta^\pi_{\tau(t+1)}(i)$ expresses the effective differences in an orthonormal basis of $\Delta_{t+1}$, and $K$ is $K_{t+1}$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The cone $K$ is written as the dual (`ConvexOptimization.dualCone`) of the simplicial cone generated by the $g_i$, which is the set displayed above. Vectors are indexed by `Fin p` (0-based), so the separation hypothesis is imposed for Lean indices $i\ge1$. The page's (B-8) is stated inside the proof of Lemma 10 for $K_{t+1}$, $p=\dim\Delta_{t+1}$; the hypotheses here are those the proof uses (Lemma B-4's (B-14)), and linear independence follows from them.
-- source:
--   Besbes, Fonseca, Lobel, Contextual Inverse Optimization: Offline and Online Learning, arXiv:2106.14015v3, p. App-19, proof of Lemma 10, (B-8); App-20 (g_i = B_Δ δ_i, (B-14))

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_CtxInvOpt_PolyCone_Cones
import Definitions.Def_dualCone

namespace CtxInvOpt.PolyCone

/-- **(B-8), arXiv:2106.14015v3, App-19 (proof of Lemma 10).** Let `0 < η ≤ 1` and let
`g_0, …, g_{p-1}` be unit vectors of `ℝ^p`, `p ≥ 1`, each `g_i` with `i ≥ 1` having squared residual at
least `η²` after projection on `span{g_0, …, g_{i-1}}` (B-14). Then the cone
`K = {c ∈ ℝ^p : c′g_i ≥ 0 ∀ i}` has circumradius `µ(K) = sin α(K) ≤ √(1 − η^{2(p−1)}/p³)`. -/
theorem eqB8_circumradius_bound {p : ℕ} (hp : 1 ≤ p) (η : ℝ) (hη0 : 0 < η) (hη1 : η ≤ 1)
    (g : Fin p → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin p)) (hunit : ∀ i, ‖g i‖ = 1)
    (hsep : ∀ i : Fin p, 0 < i.val →
      η ^ 2 ≤ ‖g i - (Submodule.span ℝ (g '' {j | j < i})).starProjection (g i)‖ ^ 2) :
    circumradius (ConvexOptimization.dualCone (simplicialCone g)) ≤
      Real.sqrt (1 - η ^ (2 * (p - 1)) / (p : ℝ) ^ 3) := by sorry

end CtxInvOpt.PolyCone
